Third-party material

The files src/ngsl.txt and src/nawl.txt, and the copies of them built into
index.html, are the New General Service List (version 1.2) and the New Academic
Word List (version 1.2) by Charles Browne, Brent Culligan and Joseph Phillips
(https://www.newgeneralservicelist.com/). They are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), not
under the MIT licence above.

The files in model/ are used only by the optional meaning model and keep their
own licences: the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 sentence-embedding model (ONNX conversion
published as Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, from sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2)
is licensed under Apache-2.0; Transformers.js (model/lib/transformers.min.js) is
licensed under Apache-2.0; and ONNX Runtime Web
(model/lib/ort-wasm-simd-threaded.jsep.wasm, and the parts of it bundled in
Transformers.js) is licensed under the MIT licence by Microsoft Corporation.

The files in data/ are third-party word lists and word norms and keep their own
licences, which are set out in data/README.md. In brief: data/lists/dale-chall.txt
(from github.com/words/dale-chall) and data/lists/excess_words.csv (from
github.com/berenslab/llm-excess-vocab; Kobak et al. 2025) are MIT-licensed, as are
the copies of them in src/dalechall.txt and src/excess.txt and in index.html. The
four files in data/norms/ are NOT under the MIT licence: the concreteness norms
(Brysbaert, Warriner & Kuperman 2014), the age-of-acquisition norms (Kuperman,
Stadthagen-Gonzalez & Brysbaert 2012) and SUBTLEX-US (Brysbaert & New 2009) are
licensed CC BY-NC-ND 3.0, and the word prevalence norms (Brysbaert, Mandera,
McCormick & Keuleers 2019) are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. They are for
non-commercial use, are loaded only on request, and can be deleted without
affecting the rest of the application.
